research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-10847-L2 -> cor-mean-value-theorem [Statement;5]: **Continuity on the closed interval cannot be dropped.** Differentiability at every point of $(a,b)$ alone does not suffice: a function on $[0,1]$, differentiable at every point of $(0,1)$ with derivative constantly $1$, for which no $c$ works, is exhibited later on this page as a false statement, a
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-10848-L2 -> cor-power-series-sums-are-continuous [Statement;2]: If $f(x)=\sum_{n\ge0}a_n(x-c)^n$ for $|x-c|<R$, then $f$ is continuous at every $x_0$ satisfying $|x_0-c|<R$.
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-10849-L2 -> lem-exponential-series-has-infinite-radius [Statement;5]: For every real $x$, the series $\sum_{n\ge0}x^n/\iota(n!)$ converges absolutely. Its power-series radius is therefore $+\infty$.
